# must-fail: expected exit code 0, got 1
#
# The anchor of the suite: it asserts nothing about a directive, only that the
# runner still judges what it declared. cat on an absent operand exits 1 against
# a declared 0. A runner that stops evaluating expect=exit:code= turns this file
# green, and every .ci that rests on an exit code with it.
#
# The child is /bin/cat rather than /bin/false, which recent macOS releases ship
# at /usr/bin/false only (the same portability trap noopBinary records in
# internal/test/fixture/install_fixture.go). The absent operand is a path no
# checkout holds, and POSIX gives cat exit 1 for an operand it cannot open, so
# the stimulus is the same non-zero exit on every host the suite runs on.

option=timeout:value=20s
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=/bin/cat /nonexistent-path-this-fixture-needs-absent
expect=exit:code=0
